# Loading & Failure UI

## Loading → `LoadingHelper` only

Use `lib/app/helpers/loading_helper.dart`. Do not use raw `CircularProgressIndicator`, SpinKit, or custom loaders in screens/widgets.

| Situation | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| Inline / button loader | `LoadingHelper.circular(context)` |
| Centered page loader | `LoadingHelper.circularCentered(context)` |
| Full-screen blocking | `LoadingHelper.overlay(context)` |
| Soft SpinKit (no overlay) | `LoadingHelper.spinKit(context)` |
| List pagination footer | `LoadingHelper.pagination(context)` |

```dart
// ❌ BAD
CircularProgressIndicator(color: ...)

// ✅ GOOD
LoadingHelper.circularCentered(context)
// or
LoadingHelper.overlay(context)
```

## Failure UI → `FailureX` only

Use `lib/app/utils/extensions/failure_extensions.dart`. Never switch on `Failure` types in UI, and never show SnackBar / Toast / Dialog / custom error text for a `Failure` manually.

| Situation | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| Transient / action error | `failure.showToast(context)` |
| Full-screen / body error | `failure.appErrorWidget(context, onPress: retry)` |

```dart
// ❌ BAD
ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(...);
// or custom if (failure is NetworkFailure) ...

// ✅ GOOD
state.failure.showToast(context);
// or
state.failure.appErrorWidget(context, onPress: () => cubit.retry());
```

Do not construct `AppErrorWidget` or call `ToastHelper` directly for `Failure` handling — go through `FailureX`.
